        }
      ],
      "content": "nail (see also clavus) | nail (cf. clavus) | nail | nails 481, 484 (see also clavus) | nail for making brigandines, body-armor for foot-soldiers made of iron rings or small thin iron plates sewn onto canvas, linen or leather and covered with a similar material. Originally in pairs (front and back), ergo often in the plural (OED s.v. brigandine) | 25, | arming-nail, forming part of armor (OED arming vgl. n. 1b) | nail for making brigandyns | middle quality nails"
    }
  ],
